WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.100
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, I finally had
a chance to see the new Godzilla so I wanted

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.410
to do a review.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.610
The closest thing we’ve had to a kaiju film
recently has been Pacific Rim, which was like

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.209
Guillermo Del Toro’s love letter to Godzilla.

00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:17.920
But this new movie is something of a reboot.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.670
So I’ll do a super quick breakdown of where
it fits with the rest of the Godzilla movies.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.870
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do movie review for all my favorite sci

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.720
fi and fantasy stuff like Days of Future Past,
Maleficent and How To Train Your Dragon 2.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.940
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.579
And if there’s a movie you really want me
to do a video for just let me know in the

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:34.579
comments.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:35.579
So before my review.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:37.970
Here’s a quick breakdown of where the new
Godzilla fits in the franchise.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:43.540
It’s kind of a spiritual sequel to the original
1954 Godzilla movie.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.790
Not really a direct sequel, but it presents
the events of the first film as a real life

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:53.010
historical event and combines that story with
things that happened in US Military History.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.170
We can talk more about that during spoilers.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.950
But for all intents and purposes this movie
pays homage to a lot of the other Godzilla

00:00:58.950 --> 00:00:59.950
movies.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.580
You don’t have to have seen any of them
to understand what’s going on though.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:08.399
But if you’re a huge Godzilla fan you’ll
notice all the bits from the older movies

00:01:08.399 --> 00:01:16.630
that they used as names for things in the
new movie.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:22.359
So because the movie is just being released
I’m going to do a non-spoilery review first

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:27.579
and then do a spoilery part where I talk about
future sequels and specific events from the

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:28.579
movie.

00:01:28.579 --> 00:01:32.389
Right off the bat Godzilla, I loved the way
he was depicted in the movie, both as part

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:34.389
of the story and visually with the effects.

00:01:34.389 --> 00:01:38.740
He’s the star, but I noticed a lot of people
were surprised by the amount of screen time

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:43.250
he got and I saw some criticism from hardcore
japanese audiences on his look.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.109
I understand where a lot of complaints come
from, especially given the way he was shown

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:48.569
in all the previous movies.

00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:52.819
But I thought what they did totally worked
and did a good job of setting up potential

00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:53.819
sequels.

00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:55.779
Which by all accounts will definitely be happening.

00:01:55.779 --> 00:01:58.009
Right now the movie is crushing it at the
box office.

00:01:58.009 --> 00:01:59.009
So it seems like it’s going to be extremely
successful.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:00.729
And we all know what happens in the movie
world.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:03.929
If it makes a ton of money, then there will
always be a sequel.

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:08.789
In terms of the non-Godzilla actors in the
movie, Bryan Cranston was great.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:11.890
Breaking Bad has been off the air long enough
that I wasn’t thinking Walter White every

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.090
minute he was on screen.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.700
Aaron Taylor Johnson and Elizabeth Olsen were
a little surreal.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.560
In case you didn’t see Winter Soldier.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.070
They’re playing Quicksilver and Scarlet
Witch in Avengers 2.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.820
So they’re brother and sister.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:28.820
And in Godzilla they were a married couple.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.480
All the X-Men Comic Fans can let me know if
they felt weird watching them be married.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.730
I think my favorite person was Ken Watanabe.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:39.810
I’ll talk more about his character in spoilers.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.000
But I just love the mythology he brought to
the story.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.360
The movie itself was pretty upfront about
what it is.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.410
A disaster event movie.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.920
It’s not like a psychological exploration
of Godzilla’s motivation.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.280
If you want that kind of movie though.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.820
Re-Watch Ang Lee’s Hulk Movie.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.320
Which was made by Universal a company that
originated a lot of the monster movies like

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.730
Dracula and Frankenstein.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.620
I didn’t consider the film to be an origin
story, just because the plot treats the original

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.270
godzilla movie in 1954 as a real life event.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.340
But I do think it’s something of a reboot
from a visual perspective.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.490
If we’re just talking about the logic, you
know, explaining how Godzilla can exist today.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.180
I think all of the Godzilla films have operated
from the idea that he is a prehistoric creature

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:26.690
that adapted biologically to deal with intense
amounts of radiation.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.380
If you’re brand new to the franchise there
might be a few things you’re confused by.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:33.200
Mostly as to how Godzilla could have survived
for millions of years.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.151
As a biological organism, at some point he’d
have to age and die.

00:03:36.151 --> 00:03:38.750
I didn’t take issue with any of the logic.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.240
I try to operate based on the rules movies
present.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.290
Like if you can grow as big as godzilla, and
you’re a reptile.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.510
Maybe you can hibernate for millions of years
too.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:50.460
I don’t like to nit pick things like that.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:56.120
Overall I gave the movie a solid B plus as
a fun monster disaster movie that did a great

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.459
job of reinvigorating the franchise.

00:03:58.459 --> 00:04:00.650
That was really the task it had to perform.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.910
Make people excited to see Godzilla movies
again in a big way.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.940
And it totally accomplished that.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:09.400
So let’s drill in to specifics and some
of my favorite moments.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.990
So careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the movie yet.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:11.990
But here are my top 5 moments.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:15.180
Number 5 - Ken Watanabe discovers the first
nest

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.470
The did a great job of hiding the fact there
were multiple monsters.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.379
So I loved when they found the Muto lair inside
the Godzilla skeleton.

00:04:22.379 --> 00:04:24.330
If you were confused by this.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:29.790
They basically said that whatever that dead
skeleton was, it was a creature that gave

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.830
off radiation that the Muto’s fed on a long
time ago.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.539
A Muto killed it, then laid it’s eggs inside
the animal so that they could feed on the

00:04:37.539 --> 00:04:38.539
radiation.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:42.050
Like with the lair and the bomb later in the
movie.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.969
Number 4 - The Male Muto hatches

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:49.430
It’s like the world coolest science experiment,
waiting for a monster chicken egg to hatch.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.940
I loved the science behind it too.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.150
The creature feeding on radiation for 15 years
in it’s cocoon, until it hatched into a

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.469
beautiful butterfly of death and desctruction.

00:04:57.469 --> 00:05:00.479
Number 3 - The Muto Mating Ritual

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:02.419
Part of me thinks that these animals aren’t
evil.

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:06.080
They’re only doing what they naturally do,
eat things and reproduce.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.379
Kill Predators.

00:05:07.379 --> 00:05:14.680
I wonder if the DVD special features will
describe some of the science of how they reproduce.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.639
Maybe if we ask Emily Grasile on brainscroop
she can tell us how animals like that would

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:19.650
reproduce.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.590
Number 2 - Godzilla History

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:26.340
I’m talking about the way they present historical
facts as if they were true.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.229
Like the atomic bomb tests in the pacific
in 1954.

00:05:29.229 --> 00:05:34.830
They invoke the Hiroshima bomb, but that one
they don’t tie to a Godzilla attack.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.270
I also really liked the way Ken Watanabe mythologized
Godzilla as this warrior for balance.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:43.350
He’s a hero, just not for mankind, he’s
fighting on the side of nature.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.710
So that makes me wonder at some point if he
could attack man, like if they ever worked

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:50.430
mechagodzilla into the new franchise.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:55.770
and my Number 1 moment - Godzilla Versus the
Mutos

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.349
It was a great action scene that pushed all
the right fan buttons.

00:05:59.349 --> 00:06:03.500
We saw Godzilla’s nuclear breath, he got
some really awesome close up moments.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.639
I really loved Godzilla furrowing his brow.

00:06:06.639 --> 00:06:10.340
Like he’s trying to do a schwarzenegger
one-liner but can’t form the words.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.110
But I also loved the way they filmed the fight
scene.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:19.309
They did a good job depicting scale and not
showing you so much of the monsters that it

00:06:19.309 --> 00:06:20.330
looked silly.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.610
But there was this one point when I thought
it looked kind of like a model.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:28.250
Like they paid homage to the original Godzilla
battles by making some of it look like three

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.940
rubber suits fighting in a model.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:37.160
Just as a bonus, my favorite non-Godzilla
scene was they 2001 Space Odyssey moment when

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.310
they all jump out of the plane and you see
their red trails of smoke passing through

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.650
the city scape.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.719
It was so beautiful, it was like a painting.

00:06:43.719 --> 00:06:44.720
If you didn’t hear it.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.759
They used that famous audio track from 2001
Space Odyssey that plays when Dave the Astronaut

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:50.889
is passing through dimensions.

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.189
I guess maybe that tied for my favorite moment.

00:06:52.189 --> 00:06:53.319
Just because I’m such a fan of 2001.

00:06:53.319 --> 00:06:55.310
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was?

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.720
And were there any easter eggs that you really
liked.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:00.599
Just to talk about sequels.

00:07:00.599 --> 00:07:04.789
Since Godzilla didn’t die at the end I don’t
expect them to do son of Godzilla anytime

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:05.789
soon.

00:07:05.789 --> 00:07:07.879
But I do want to see a mech.

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:10.319
Maybe not a straight up mechagodzilla.

00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:13.669
But now that everyone knows about Godzilla,
how can the governments of the world NOT build

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:15.039
a countermeasure.

00:07:15.039 --> 00:07:20.689
They mythologized the prehistoric creatures
in a pretty clear way, so I think the next

00:07:20.689 --> 00:07:23.379
film will just feature another creature like
Mothra and a third one.

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:27.370
Let me know which Godzilla monsters you want
to see next!

